Platform: two-socket Xeon 6960P (Granite Rapids, Xeon 6 P-core) server in SNC3:
six NUMA nodes, four DSA and four IAA per socket (one work queue each configured
on the first pair of each socket), AMX with FP16, RDT allocation.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- Xeon 6960P: 72 cores / 144 threads, 2S, QAT/DLB/DSA/IAA "4 default devices",
  Intel RDT Yes: https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/240775/intel-xeon-6960p-processor-432m-cache-2-70-ghz/specifications.html
- SNC: arch/x86/kernel/cpu/resctrl/monitor.c snc_get_config() (CPUs sharing CPU 0's
  L3 / CPUs in CPU 0's node; GRANITERAPIDS_X is in snc_cpu_ids), so cpu0's
  cache/index3/shared_cpu_list spans the socket (144 CPUs) and node0 holds 48.
- /sys/devices/system/node/node<N>/cpulist, cpu<N>/topology/physical_package_id,
  cache/index3/shared_cpu_list, PCI numa_node: Documentation/ABI/stable/sysfs-devices-node,
  Documentation/ABI/stable/sysfs-devices-system-cpu, Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-pci.
- DSA 0x0b25 / IAA 0x0cfe on idxd: include/linux/pci_ids.h, drivers/dma/idxd/init.c.
  idxd's id table has no Granite Rapids-SP entry of its own (only SPR0, GNRD, DMR,
  PTL, WCL), so these devices are given the SPR ids it binds; inferred from that
  table, not captured. dsa<n>/iax<n> and wq<dev>.<n> naming as in xeon-spr-accel.
- amx_fp16 (12*32+21), rdt_a, cat_l3, cdp_l3, mba, avx_vnni: arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeatures.h.

Layout: sysfs paths and relative symlinks follow the driver core's naming, in
exactly the form tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes (the matrix test re-captures each
tree and requires an identical result).

Not from hardware: the CPU numbering (cores 0-143 by socket, SMT siblings +144),
BDFs, the node-to-device placement, char-device minors, the kernel release string,
the brand string in model name (built from the ARK processor number) and the
cpuinfo flags line (a subset in cpufeatures.h order).
QAT is left out: the PCI id Granite Rapids' QAT enumerates as is not in a primary
source read for this fixture (qat-420xx covers the 420xx PF), so doctor reports
QAT 0 of the ARK default per socket.
